Below are the next steps to take for various development pipelines.

Tile improvement and working:
 - We will need an effect type that boost tile improvement yields; e.g. "Gunpowder Blasting" for Mines.
 - We need the tile selector to return tiles that will be worked that miss improvements; this is to help the AI trigger draft workers.
 - We need a condition for terminating and returning draft workers.
 - We might want a second stage to mk01-general draft workers that add a few unworked improvements at the end of its run. 
 - Make sure the improvement yield boost lookup table is moved to data IO.   
 - We will need a O(1) lookup structure for effects pertaining to tile improvement yields.


Static data:
 - Need to implement dynamic enums for those cases when the hot-path need to lookup static data without a string compare. 


Map generation:
 - We currently place some resources on water, or on mountains, that should not be placed there (see aux_res_imp_terrain_comp).